               DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION ANNOUNCES
               FIRST DIGITAL CONTENT CENTER FOR DESIGN
           AND DELIVERY OF INTERACTIVE MEDIA APPLICATIONS


  Location in Metropolitan New York Will Support Content Providers of
                   Video and Interactive Services


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 31, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the establishment of its first Digital Content 
Center, located in Tarrytown, New York.  The Center is intended to 
support the design and development of interactive video applications 
and services for video and interactive services pilots and 
deployments throughout North America.

     "The Digital Content Center will actively link video and 
interactive services content providers with video service 
distribution partners worldwide. It will deliver a full range of 
services and support to organizations seeking efficient ways to 
provide interactive information to consumers," said Charles F. 
Christ, vice president of Digital Equipment Corporation's Storage 
Business Unit and the company's Video and Interactive Information 
Services group.  "Now, in addition to delivering the industry's 
leading end-to-end video and interactive information server 
solution, Digital is offering the means to design, develop and 
implement the creation of media applications for interactive 
services."

     According to Phil Corman, manager of the Digital Content Center 
program, Digital's new Content Center provides the technology and 
services to develop,distribute and manage a variety of new 
interactive media applications.  Said Corman, "Digital is unique in 
offering a totally seamless solution for content providers that 
encompasses encoding of video and audio, non-linear editing, and
authoring."

The Digital Content Center will provide such services as:

     -	Planning, design and development of interactive applications 
        including video-on-demand, news-on-demand, interactive 
        shopping, interactive business information, distance 
        learning applications, and others.

     -	Digitization and compression of video and audio, initially 
        using MPEG-1 technology, and moving to MPEG-2 when 
        available, while offering backward compatibility with 
        MPEG-1.

     -	End-to-end testing of interactive applications in actual 
        interactive video service provider networks.

     -	Training and consulting services for content providers and 
        developers to design and develop interactive applications 
        for various set-top environments.

     -	Integration services to link new interactive applications 
        with existing databases and processes.


     The Digital Content Center will begin operations in Tarrytown, 
New York, in summer, 1994, with plans to establish multiple Centers 
throughout the world.  Digital also announced that it will make its 
technology platform available to large-scale content providers who 
wish to own and operate their own content production centers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
