                DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW REDUCED PRICES
                    FOR ALPHA AXP MICROPROCESSORS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 6, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced new reduced prices for its high-performance Alpha 
AXP microprocessor family. The announcement underscores Digital's 
commitment to continue to offer the industry's most powerful
microprocessors at competitive prices.

     Ed Caldwell, vice president of Semiconductor Operations, 
said the new reduced prices "are indicative of Digital's strong 
commitment to the merchant semiconductor market.  Alpha AXP 
microprocessors are the world's highest-performance family of 
microprocessors.  The 21064A-275MHz chip is the most powerful in
the industry."

     Digital also announced the 21064A-233MHz Alpha AXP 
microprocessor to replace the previously introduced 225MHz version.  
The higher clock rate optimizes performance with the 33MHz 21071 and 
21072 PCI-based system logic chips that Digital introduced in 
January.  The following new prices, per chip in quantities of 5,000, 
will be effective July 3, 1994:  

           Model                          Price (US List)

           Alpha AXP 21068-66MHz          $   186
           Alpha AXP 21066-166MHz         $   347
           Alpha AXP 21064-166MHz         $   404
           Alpha AXP 21064-200MHz         $   544
           Alpha AXP 21064A-233MHz        $   788
           Alpha AXP 21064A-275MHz        $ 1,083

     The market focus for Alpha AXP microprocessors is on high-
performance Windows NT client and server applications.  With Alpha 
AXP chips, system manufacturers can develop cost-effective, high-
performance solutions that customers want for performance-demanding  
applications in electronic and mechanical computer-aided design 
(CAD), computer-aided software engineering (CASE), multimedia, 
imaging and graphics, publishing, and database management. Digital 
continues to offer the highest performing microprocessors in the 
industry (see chart below).

