          DIGITAL ANNOUNCES HEDIS REPORTING PLATFORM (HRP)


   Client/server system helps users access new and existing data 


MIAMI BEACH, FL -- June 6, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the Digital Health Plan Employer Data and 
Information Set (HEDIS) Reporting Platform (HRP), a packaged 
solution including hardware and software, applications and services 
that directly resolve significant challenges customers face in 
complying with the HEDIS 2.0 performance standards. 

     HEDIS is a standard reporting set of performance measures 
showing value and accountability of a health plan to an employer 
group.  Digital's announcement was made at the Group Health 
Association of America (GHAA) conference. Digital also announced its 
partnership with Codman Research Group to create the HEDIS Reporting 
Platform. PANDORA Managed Care Information System, from Codman, is 
the data analysis and reporting application. 

     More and more employer groups are demanding HEDIS reporting
from their managed care providers. HEDIS reporting focuses on 4 
major areas of performance:  quality, access and patient 
satisfaction, membership, and utilization and finance.  Reporting on 
these areas is difficult because the data resides on disparate 
systems/applications, and even in a paper form, the environments are 
networked but not integrated, and access to the data is difficult.  
Teams of individuals are required to manually gather HEDIS reporting 
information. Data access, automation and integration have become key 
business needs in order to reduce time and costs.

     "Because Digital helped create the HEDIS data standard, we can 
help customers establish a true 'apples to apples' HEDIS reporting 
system," said David Samuel, HEDIS program manager for Digital's  
Healthcare Business Segment.  "HRP creates a seamless, client/server 
system and data warehouse environment to access the needed data.  We 
can help reengineer the business processes to capture relevant new 
data automatically.  The solution provides customers with a powerful 
tool for generating and formatting HEDIS reports for employers, and 
a clear audit trail for the National Committee for Quality Assurance 
(NCQA)."

     "Just about everybody, health plans and employers alike, agrees 
that standardized reporting of quality data will drive major 
improvements in patient care and help contain costs through 
competitive marketplace pressures," said Kathleen Angel, Digital's 
corporate benefits manager. "The most important result will be a 
consistent improvement in the quality of health care." 
Developing a HEDIS report is resource intensive.  Data needed often 
is either not available, not accessible or not integrated.   
Digital's HRP solution takes advantage of Digital's client/server 
Alpha AXP technology, networking and integration and a unique 
application from an industry leading business partner. The HEDIS 
Reporting System solution allows you to capture and access HEDIS 
data effectively and efficiently.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, helps 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
