             DIGITAL ANNOUNCES FIVE NEW PC PRINTERS


ATLANTA, GA -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced five new low-cost personal printers for direct 
connection to PCs.  The printers include color ink jet, 
monochrome and color dot matrix and laser models priced between 
$199 and $779.  All ship with Windows drivers.  The announcement 
was made at the Windows World Conference, which opened here today 
at the Georgia World Congress Center.

     "Today's announcement of a new line of PC printers clearly 
positions Digital as a contender in the growing market for PC 
peripherals," said Larry Cabrinety, Vice President of Digital's 
Components and Peripherals Business Unit.  "Our decision to 
launch these products through distributors or retailers 
demonstrates our strategy of open business practices with 
competitive products which are easy to buy."

     All five printers are currently available.  The new family 
includes:

     o The DECcolorwriter 520ic printer, a color ink jet with Color 
       Write Out of the Box; 5 pages-per-minute text performance, 
       separate color and monochrome ink cartridges, priced at $449.

     o The DECwriter 500i printer, a monochrome ink jet with 5 ppm 
       performance and optional color capability, priced at $399.

     o The DECwriter 65 printer, a 24-wire narrow-carriage dot matrix 
       with Color Write Out of the Box; 2 ppm text performance priced at 
       $229.

     o The DECwriter 55 printer, a 24-wire narrow-carriage dot matrix 
       priced at $199.

     o The DEClaser 1800 printer, a 6 ppm 300 X 300 dpi laser with 
       U.S. EPA Energy Star compliance, priced at $779.

