              JEANETTE HORAN APPOINTED GROUP MANAGER OF
          DIGITAL'S EMERGING NETWORK TECHNOLOGIES DIVISION
 

NEW ORLEANS, LA -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the appointment of Jeanette Horan to the position of 
Group Manager of its Emerging Network Technologies Division within 
the Network Product Business.  Ms. Horan assumes direct business 
responsibility for growing new revenue streams based on the business 
viability of selected new networking technologies and markets in 
four key areas: cable television data communication, 
telecollaboration, mobile and wireless communications. 

     Most recently, Ms. Horan was vice president of interoperable 
technologies at the Open Software Foundation, where she was also a 
member of the organization's executive strategy committee.  Her 
accomplishments include managing the timely development of 
commercial products, identifying customer requirements and directing 
the operations of engineering teams. 

     "She brings to Digital more than 17 years of experience and 
leadership managing complex development projects, many of which 
required building cohesive alliances between participants with 
diverse perspectives," said Laurence Walker, vice president and 
general manager of the Network Product Business. 

     "I'm fascinated by the challenge of creating and applying 
technologies in new markets," said Ms. Horan.  "In terms of product 
development, this gives us an incredible opportunity to create 
offerings that break new ground -- from using cable television
networks for fast data transfer, to helping make real-time 
interactive data communications a reality at the desktop."

     Ms. Horan will work closely with each of the product 
development teams in the 65-person division.  She will also help to 
establish strategic relationships with key service providers and 
value added resellers that currently address these core markets. 

     "We're all in the business of providing information," she said.  
"We have an opportunity to work with new partners, like cable 
television companies, and develop new solutions -- such as using 
bridges developed by Digital to send data across other companies' 
cable networks.  As a leader in the networks business, Digital can 
share its expertise with our partners in the cable industry.  I look
forward to forging these partnerships, which will lead us in very 
exciting directions."

     Prior to her position as vice president at  the Open Systems 
Foundation, Ms. Horan was the director of software engineering for 
Gould Computer Systems Division, which was acquired by Encore 
Computer Corp.  She began her computing career as a programmer for 
the British Link Miles division of Singer.  Ms. Horan received her 
bachelor's of science degree from the University of London, and an
M.B.A. from Boston University. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
                                ####

