            CONVERGENCE SYSTEMS INC. ALIGNS WITH DIGITAL
                 TO RESELL CHANNELWORKS PRODUCT LINE


      Systems Integrator Will Help Cable TV Companies Worldwide
        Target New Markets for High-Speed Data Communications

 
NEW ORLEANS, LA -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced an agreement with Convergence Systems, Inc. (CSI) to 
become the first authorized reseller for its ChannelWorks products.  
As the first in a series of products, the award-winning ChannelWorks 
bridge provides users with the enabling technology to economically
send and receive diverse data over existing cable television lines, 
thereby solving the "last mile" problem of connection to the 
information superhighway.

     "Cable television networks are perfect for data networking," 
said David Wood, president of CSI.  "Enabled by ChannelWorks 
technology, cable networks can provide two-way communication, with 
bandwidth that can support multimedia applications such as video 
teleconferencing.  For users, the biggest benefit is that everyone 
located within a metropolitan area network can communicate with 
others in that area increasing accessibility to shared documents and 
databases, as well as high-bandwidth applications like shared 
CAD/CAM."

     Launched by former Digital employees who had spent the past 
several years consulting with the industry's leading cable 
operators, CSI specializes in supporting the communications 
industry.  CSI's chairman, David R. Ames, also has substantial 
experience in the entertainment and multimedia arenas.

     "We're very pleased to welcome CSI to our ranks of system 
integrators," said Art Zins, business segment manager of the 
Emerging Network Technologies Division, which develops the 
ChannelWorks products.  "They're focused on our core market and 
bring a wealth of knowledge about and experience with the cable 
industry.  We know they can support our customers, and their 
extensive background in Digital's products and network integration 
gives them tremendous strength."

     CSI provides network design, installation, integration and 
consulting services to clients worldwide.  A current CSI project 
with Time-Warner's cable television company in Hawaii will use 
Digital's ChannelWorks bridges throughout the state to allow school
administrators and teachers at more than 300 facilities to share a 
variety of information and introduce multimedia instruction to K-12 
class rooms.  Administrators will use the network to speed routine 
tasks, like attendance records.  Future plans call for the school
system's libraries to develop an integrated on-line catalog, which 
will speed transfers of reference materials throughout the state.  
The network will also allow teachers and administrators to schedule 
video conferences, in lieu of face-to-face meetings.

     "Everyone's just beginning to explore how they can use cable 
lines for broadband data communications," said Wood. "We'll help 
the cable companies explore these new business opportunities.  And 
we'll help organizations use these networks to cut their costs 
associated with data communication, by using the metropolitan area 
networks the cable companies have already put in place."

     Two of CSI's target markets are healthcare and education.  
Schools are using cable TV to provide distance learning, in which a 
teacher and several students share a video classroom.  They are also 
eager to incorporate multimedia applications, and need cable's 
larger capacity to carry video signals.  Similarly, healthcare 
institutions are pursuing cable TV to carry digitized images of 
X-rays and other patient records to physicians and researchers.  
These teams are often located in a in a common medical center, which 
offers easy access to existing cable networks.

     Other solutions CSI offers include: entertainment, news and 
media, retail and electronic commerce, financial services and 
insurance, travel, and government.

     CSI is headquartered in Atlanta with offices in Palo Alto, 
Dallas and Rochester, N.Y.  Its staff works closely with Digital's 
direct sales force to sell the ChannelWorks products and provide 
ongoing support.  Digital expects to announce additional resellers 
of ChannelWorks offerings in the future.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
