          DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW VERSION OF LAT PROTOCOL
                      WITH X WINDOW SUPPORT


ATLANTA, GA  -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced a new version of the LAT protocol  with added support for 
X Window terminals and PCs running X-Terminal emulation.  Improved 
network performance also has been added.  The announcement was made 
at the Windows World Conference, which opened here today at the 
Georgia World Congress Center.

     The LAT protocol supports communications between terminal  
servers and host computer systems with terminals, PCs and printers 
over local area networks.   With this latest LAT announcement, 
Digital is demonstrating its commitment to continue LAT as the 
premiere network protocol to connect terminals and printers to the 
local area network.  Digital licenses the LAT protocol to terminal 
server, host, computer software and protocol analyzer vendors, the 
vast majority of whom use it in their networks.

     The new V5.2.2 version of the LAT protocol enables licensees 
to build products that implement X Windows over LAT.  These 
products include X Window terminals and PCs running X-terminal 
emulation.

     "This expansion of the LAT protocol to support X Window 
terminals adds the features needed for X Windows terminals to run 
the growing number of X-based applications over the LAT protocol," 
said Larry Cabrinety, Vice President of Digital's Components and 
Peripherals Business Unit.  "Our commitment to actively license 
this protocol to all vendors involved with X Windows demonstrates 
Digital's open systems strategy."

     The four new features of the LAT V5.2.2 protocol are Delayed 
Acknowledgment, to decrease network traffic by allowing hosts to 
delay the acknowledgment of LAT packets; LAT Service Class 3, to 
allow licensees to build products that implement X Windows over 
LAT; LAT Service Class 4 to provide font services to X Window 
terminals using LAT; and Host Initiated Connection Security to 
handle solicited connections to terminal server ports having 
password protected services.

     Previous LAT features retained in the current version include 
host load balancing, session multiplexing, automatic addressing and 
interoperability.  Digital provides certain features of the new 
version of LAT to existing licensees at no charge.  Support for X 
Window terminals and X Window terminal emulation software over LAT 
is available as an addendum to the LAT license for a separate fee.

     Digital Equipment Corporation, is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
