    PC MANUFACTURERS CAN NOW ENTER THE EMERGING RISC PC MARKET
 QUICKLY AND COST-EFFECTIVELY WITH NEW OEM INCENTIVE PROGRAM FROM 
                     DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORP.


WINDOWS WORLD, ATLANTA, GEORGIA, May 23, 1994 -- Those eager to 
capitalize on the merging RISC PC market -- which is projected to 
total $7.4 billion by 1995 according to San Jose, CA-based market 
research firm Dataquest, Inc., -- can now enter this sector 
rapidly with a minimal development investment via a new OEM 
incentive program from Digital Equipment Corporation.  Known at 
the OEMbedded First Program, this aggressive initiative from 
Digital's Component OEM Group allows original equipment 
manufacturers (OEMs) to access Alpha AXP 64-bit RISC technology 
at all levels of integration, including chips, boards, and a 
complete line of client and server systems for private label.  
Furthermore, the OEMbedded First Program options will offer the 
industry's most competitive price/performance ratios, allowing 
OEMs to market highly aggressive product lines that can compete 
effectively against lower-performance DOS-based offerings.

     The OEMbedded First Program offers three separate support 
programs, 1. rapid technology acquisition; 2.  integration and 
contract manufacturing services; and, 3.  market development 
resources, each designed to provide a rapid ascension for OEMs 
entering a new market with highly advanced, competitive 
technology.  As a three-tier program, OEMbedded First targets 
three types of OEM "RISC PC early adopters:"  1. Industry-First 
Leaders;  2. Price/Performance Innovators; and,  3. High-Concept 
Developers.  

     According to Mike Ritz, the Alpha AXP OEM business manager, 
this Program represents the industry's first aggressive RISC PC 
ramp-up designed exclusively for OEMs.  "Today, OEMs face 
tremendous risks when they enter new, emerging markets with 
advanced product lines not regularly used by their customer base.  
Therefore, Digital has developed OEM support programs designed to 
minimize the investment risk as well as attract new markets still 
untapped by many PC vendors.  The OEMbedded First initiative 
fully supports the competitiveness and uniqueness of the Alpha/NT 
RISC PC platform, positioning our OEMs on a higher playing field 
above their competitors marketing lower performance DOS- and 
PowerPC-based platforms."

     "The Alpha AXP architecture offers the best performance for 
RISC PC platforms," said Dominic Ricchetti, Director and 
Principal Analyst of the Workstation Worldwide Programs at 
Dataquest, Inc.  

     "In addition, the scalability of Alpha AXP's 64-bit RISC 
architecture ensures excellent competitiveness for OEMs to 
differentiate now and in their next generation products," said 
Ricchetti.   

     Another incentive for PC manufacturers is the OEMbedded 
First Program's Alpha AXP options that fully support nearly 6,000 
new applications -- more than two-thirds of which are based on 
Microsoft's Windows NT and DEC OSF/1 UNIX operating systems.  
According to Ritz, "the availability of NT and OSF/1 for 
commercial, mainstream applications, is a strong attraction to 
end-users seeking a higher-capacity solution."            

Dataquest Projects That RISC PC Factory Revenues Will Grow 
At A Compound Annual Growth Rate Of 200% Through 1998

     PC manufacturers faced with an overcrowded, low-margin 
32-bit DOS PC market as well as declining workstation prices, 
must diversify their product line and add value to differentiate 
themselves from competitors, said Ritz.  In addition, the growing 
end-user demand for multimedia, virtual reality, video/broadcast, 
advanced mathematics and statistical software on the desktop will 
require higher-performance PCs to handle the extra speed and 
bandwidth requirement of these more advanced, graphically-intense 
software packages.

     "RISC PC factory revenues will grow at a compound annual 
growth rate of over 200% through 1998," said Ricchetti.  This 
high growth will be fueled by the increasing demand for PCs that 
can support advanced user interfaces and new applications, 
including multimedia, video, virtual reality, CAD/CAM and 
object-oriented solutions.  

     "RISC PCs will provide a wide range of solutions, from 
advanced desktop users to server applications, with both Windows 
NT and UNIX.  Digital's relationship with Microsoft, its support 
for Windows NT integration, and its standards compliant 64-bit 
UNIX, DEC OSF/1, makes Digital a strong partner for the RISC PC 
market," he said.

OEMbedded First Program Provides Three-Tier Approach 
To Meet Specific Needs Of OEM RISC PC Early Adopters

     According to Ritz, there are three types of PC manufacturers 
that are most likely to gain the greatest benefits by entering 
the RISC PC market immediately.  These "early adopters," can be 
classified by the following three categories:

1.   The Industry-First Leader

     OEMs that wish to enter their market first with an Alpha/NT 
     platform with a minimal design and manufacturing investment;

2.   The Price/Performance Innovator

     OEMs that wish to enter their market with the industry's  
     most competitive price/performance RISC PC designs --  
     particularly OEMs that must cost-effectively add greater  
     differentiation and value to their designs.

3.   The High-Concept Developer  

     OEMs, involved in high-end markets such as graphics,  
     multimedia, broadcast, CAD/CAM, etc. that wish to create the 
     most high-performance, specialized systems in their  
     industry.  These OEMs are involved in developing  
     compute-intensive applications and their end-users are eager 
     to migrate to cost-effective, standards-based, Windows NT 	
     platforms but cannot sacrifice the performance of custom  
     designed systems.

The OEMbedded First Program provides specific product options, 
price discounts, market support programs and integration/contract 
manufacturing services to each of these three groups:

1.   Industry-First Leader Program

     Private Label Complete Alpha AXP Systems Offered At Volume 
     Discounts; Contract Manufacturing and Integration Services 
     Readily Available; Complete Market Development Data On RISC 
     PC and NT Segment Readily Available;

2.   Price/Performance Innovator Program

     Alpha AXP PC Motherboards, VME-based Single Board Computers, 
     Full PCI Options All Offered At Volume Discounts; Full Suite 
     Of Competitive Benchmarks, Positioning and Research Readily 
     Available; Complete Market Development Data On RISC PC and 
     NT Segment Readily Available; "Head Start Program" which 
     will be customized by Digital and the OEM to Provide 
     End-Users With An Early Start On Application Development.

3.   High-Concept Developer Program

     Alpha AXP Microprocessors, Workstations Available At Volume 
     Discounts; Participation In Development Of Next-Generation 
     Alpha Offerings; Integration, Consulting, Services Readily 
     Available; Complete Market Development Data On RISC PC and 
     NT Segment Readily Available.
 
New OEMbedded First Source Book Available Immediately To PC 
Manufacturers Seeking New Market And Technology Data

     Digital is providing an OEMbedded First Source Book and 
companion video tape to PC manufacturers that seek market 
development information, excerpts of new forecasts from Dataquest 
on the RISC PC segment as well as new technology and applications 
information before they enter the market sector.  Entitled, "A 
Guide to Maximizing Your Potential In the Emerging RISC PC 
Market," the OEMbedded Source Book, Version 1.0, and companion 
videotape can be ordered by calling Digital Equipment 
Corporation's Component OEM Group at 1-800-OEM-RISC with the U.S. 
and 001-508-467-7472 outside the U.S.
