         50th Anniversary of D-Day and the Battle of Normandy


       DIGITAL, EXCLUSIVE IT PARTNER OF THE "JUBILEE OF FREEDOM"


Paris, FR -- June 6, 1994 -- Digital France is providing the 
information system to manage the offering of the Jubilee of
Freedom commemorative medals to about 250,000 veterans (English,
American and Canadian). As an official sponsor of the event, the
Digital branch in Rouen will lend the necessary hardware,
software and services to the regional Council of Normandy to
present the medals to veterans during their stay in Normandy
during the anniversary. Additional Medals will be presented 
between now and the end of the year.

     In order to pay tribute to veterans of the Battle of
Normandy, the Regional Council of Normandy has created a
commemorative medal. These medals will be presented to the
veterans by mayors, regional and general councillors from
Normandy either at the Women's Abbey in Caen or on one of 1,000
battle sites chosen by the recipient.

     Digital is providing the IT system (hardware, software and
services) on which the presentation of these medals rely. The
main features of the system are:

     o constitution of the data base, with about 2,000 characters per   
       veteran. Today, the data base provides information concerning 
       20,000 veterans. 100,000 of them will receive their medals 
       before the end of the summer.

     o mailing of invitations and correspondance 

     o printing of personnalized certificate

     o administration of the approximately 1,500 officials on 1,000 
       different sites. About 30 ceremonies can be held concurrently, 
       each one organized for 30 recipients. 

     This cooperation between the Digital office in Normandy and
the Regional Council of Normandy has been made possible thanks to
a long lasting business relationship. Digital began operations in
Normandy in the early 80's and the Rouen office opened in 1986.

