                  DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION

                           FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:   DIGITAL's DISTRIBUTED QUEUING SERVICE FOR OpenVMS V1.3

OVERVIEW:

Digital's Distributed Queuing Service (DQS) enables OpenVMS users 
on any node in a DECnet network to use any OpenVMS connected 
printer anywhere in the world, as easily as they use a printer 
directly connected to their own computer.  Running on both VAX 
and Alpha AXP platforms, DQS is compatible with the user's local 
print commands, and requires no rewriting of applications.

DQS moves jobs from a queue on one system to a queue on another, 
and also manipulates jobs in the remote queue.  DQS supports all 
OpenVMS printer types, and permits users and applications to 
address remote printers as they access local printers.  It also 
supports user-written print symbionts for third-party printers 
and plotters.


KEY FEATURES AND BENEFITS:

o Provides fast, high-performance access to any printer anywhere 
  in the OpenVMS DECnet network -- both VAX and Alpha AXP 
  systems.

o Supports wide area and local area networks.

o Distributes reports to geographically distributed sites.

o Is fully compatible with standard OpenVMS print commands and   
  qualifiers.

o Protects investment.  Requires no user training and no 
  rewriting of application software.

o Enhances flexibility of network configuration.

o Provides security by enabling managers to control which systems 
  may have access to which printers.

o Supports DECnet Phase V fullname functionality.

o Implements POLYCENTER Software Installation (PCSI).

PRICING AND AVAILABILITY:

DQS V1.3 is priced between $140 and $3,943 depending upon the 
number of supported nodes.  Media and documentation are priced 
separately at $425.  Shipments begin May, 1994.

WARRANTY:

Warranty for DQS V1.3 is one year.
