               DIGITAL ANNOUNCES PACKAGED INTELLIGENT
              STACKABLE SOLUTIONS, AND PRICE REDUCTIONS
                          ON KEY COMPONENTS

     	    
MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 8, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation's 
Network Product Business today announced a comprehensive set of 
"stackable" packaged solutions and price reductions on key 
components, up to 40 percent, to reinforce its strategy in the 
intelligent "stackable" market. 

     These solutions incorporate Digital's award-winning DEChub 
products, and take advantage of the DEChub family's unique 
capability of being configurable for both stackable and multislot 
hub environments.  

     The packaged solutions include an Intelligent Stackable Starter 
Package, featuring Digital's DEChub 90 backplane and three 
DECrepeater 90Ts, as well as "Five-Packs" of DECrepeater 90Ts.  
These packages provide 10baseT Ethernet connections at a list price 
of $83 per port. The packages can be configured with other DEChub 
products such as DECagent 90 and HUBwatch for comprehensive 
manageability; and DECbrouter 90 bridge/router for remote access to 
local area network (LAN) resources.  		

     According to William L. Maro, group manager, Network 
Interconnect Product Group, "Whether it's a remote site, a small/
medium size firm, or a workgroup or department within a large 
enterprise, users have three basic networking needs:  connectivity 
of PC's and workstations; access to headquarters and regional sites; 
and network management. "Digital's industry-leading design flexibility 
provides a set of modular hubs, routers and network management tools 
that provide scalability from stackable to DEChub multislot 
configurations.  And, these solutions offer enterprise hub functionality 
at 'stackable' prices," he added.

The emergence of the stackable market

     The growth of client/server computing within workgroups, 
departments, and enterprises has resulted in the stackable hub 
market being the fastest growing segment of the intelligent hub 
market.  Increasingly, customers are recognizing the need to add 
functionality such as internetworking and network management to 
supplement basic connectivity solutions.  This has led to the 
emergence of the "intelligent stackable" market as an important high 
growth segment of the networking market.

     "The new stackables provide a more attractive option for adding 
connectivity, segmentation and new technologies to the network 
without the fear of product obsolescence," commented Melinda Le 
Baron, program director, Local Area Communications (LAC) service, 
Gartner Group.  "We believe this will be one of the driving reasons 
behind the quick shift to stackable product for new connectivity 
requirements."   

DECbrouter 90 price reduction

     Prices also have been reduced on the DECbrouter 90, a 2-port 
multiprotocol router, jointly developed by Digital and Cisco.  
Said Elaine Hodgdon, DECbrouter marketing manager, "The DECbrouter 
90 is a key component of network connectivity in general, and the 
intelligent stackable solution in particular.  It provides universal 
network access through a modular, flexible hardware design, with 
multivendor interoperability and competitive pricing, independent of 
a customer's architecture."

Product and Package Pricing
    
     Intelligent Stackable Starter Package              $1995
     (DEChub 90 plus 3 DECrepeater 90Ts)
    
     DECrepeater 90T
       -DEChub version                                  $ 895
       -Stackable version                               $1030
    
    DECrepeater 90T (5-pack packages)                   $3975
    
    DECbrouter 90
       -DEChub version                                  $3450
       -Stackable version                               $3500
    
           
     All products and packages are currently available. The starter 
and 5-pack packages are limited time offers, expiring on September 
30, 1994.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
