           DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NETWORK PRINTING SOFTWARE
                     FOR FIVE UNIX PLATFORMS


ATLANTA, GA -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced network printing software for five UNIX 
platforms:  Pyramid, Sequent, Silicon Graphics, Solaris, and 
UNISYS systems.  The network printing software enables desktop 
users in these five environments to access Digital's PrintServer 
network printers anywhere in their networks, whether local or 
remote, without the need for any other Digital hardware or 
software.  The announcement was made at the Windows World '94 
Conference, which opened here today at the Georgia World Congress 
Center.

     The new PrintServer software adds five UNIX environments to 
the platforms currently supported, which include IBM-AIX, HP-UX, 
AT&T Unison, SCO UNIX, SunOS, ULTRIX, Novell NetWare, Windows NT, 
DEC OSF/1, OpenVMS (VAX/AXP) networks, and PCs and MACS, or any 
combination of these environments.

     "The extension of Digital's network printing leadership to 
these five UNIX platforms demonstrates our commitment to open 
systems and enables additional users to access the level of 
network printing which only Digital provides," said Larry 
Cabrinety, Vice President of Digital's Components and Peripherals 
Business Unit.  "The combination of Digital's PrintServer network 
printers and software provides bi-directional real-time printer 
and print job status communication, with printers in remote 
geographies, for users of 17 different network environments.  No 
other company matches this level of network printing."

     The new PrintServer software enables Pyramid, Sequent, 
Silicon Graphics, Solaris, and UNISYS users to access any of 
Digital's PrintServer printers and benefit from such specific 
features as real-time, bi-directional communication of printer 
and print job status, remote monitoring and management of 
printers, printer accounting to enable system managers to bill 
back for printer usage, input and output tray selection, simplex 
(one-sided) and duplex (two-sided) printing, and simple ASCII, 
PCL-5 and PostScript Level 2 printing.  It provides host-based 
value-added printing such as automatic data-type detection and 
translation to PostScript.  The software requires no modification 
to existing system programs, operating system source modules, or 
the kernel.  No additional Digital hardware or software is 
required.

     The software provides formatting capabilities including 
number-up to 100 (multiple page images printed on a single side 
of paper for easier document viewing and to save paper), and 
lay-up (custom page placement on the sheet, borders, image 
scaling to fit different paper sizes, and offsetting page images 
for binding or hole punching).

     Optional fonts, forms, logos, software and future printing 
enhancements are downloaded, via a single remote system 
management facility to manage and control all PrintServer 
printers on the network.  This facility is a standard feature of 
PrintServer software.  The software provides investment 
protection of installed printers.

      The new PrintServer software is licensed with each 
PrintServer printer as part of the base price.  The license 
permits the unlimited right to copy the software within the LAN 
in which the PrintServer printer operates.  There is a one-time 
media kit/documentation charge of $300.  Traditional OpenVMS and 
ULTRIX support is also available.

     Digital's PrintServer printers that are supported on the 
five new UNIX platforms include the 17 page-per-minute, 70,000 
impression/month PrintServer 17/600 printer priced at $4,695, the 
20 page-per-minute, 70,000 impression/month turboPrintServer 20 
printer priced at $11,995 and the 32 page-per-minute, 150,000 
impression/month PrintServer 32 printer priced at $20,995.  Each 
includes Ethernet, Adobe PostScript Level 2 (PrintServer 17/600 
only), 300 X 300 dpi resolution (600 X 600 dpi on the PrintServer 
17/600), and optional duplex (standard on the turboPrintServer 20 
printer).  In addition, the PrintServer 32 printer offers 
paper-handling options including a 3000-sheet input tray and 
3000-sheet output tray (each priced at $2,995, or $2,495 if 
purchased with the printer) which allow for longer, uninterrupted 
runtimes, overnight and batch printing, and a 20-bin mailbox with 
lockable bins (priced at $9,995), to provide confidential network 
printing, even from remote geographies.

     Digital Equipment Corporation, is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
