           ATTACHMATE AND XYPLEX LICENSE MULTI-SESSION
          TECHNOLOGY FROM DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION


ATLANTA, GA -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Attachmate Corporation of Bellevue, 
Washington, and Xyplex Corporation of Littleton, Massachusetts, 
have licensed Digital's Terminal Device Session Management
Protocol (TD/SMP).  Under terms of the agreements, Attachmate has 
licensed this technology from Digital for use with its terminal 
emulator software products; Xyplex will be using it in its 
terminal server products.

     The TD/SMP protocol enables multiple terminal sessions to 
communicate with multiple processors over a single serial line.  
The protocol enables serial line connected terminals and PCs to 
display multiple sessions.   The license includes rights to use 
Digital's patents and the architectural specifications of the 
protocol.  The announcement was made at the Windows World 
Conference, which opened here today at the Georgia World Congress 
Center.

     "In the spirit of becoming the best open systems company, 
Digital is licensing this technology to any vendor who wants to 
use this protocol," said Larry Cabrinety, Vice President of 
Digital's Components and Peripherals Business Unit.  "These 
agreements demonstrate our commitment to open business 
practices."

     Terminal vendors, terminal emulation software vendors and 
terminal server vendors can make use of this technology to 
improve their products and make them compatible with Digital's.  
The TD/SMP protocol is included with Digital's OpenVMS operating 
system and selected terminals and terminal server products.

      All parties have agreed to keep the royalty rates and other 
financial terms of their respective agreements confidential.

