           DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NETWORK PRINTING SOFTWARE
                   FOR WINDOWS NT APPLICATIONS


ATLANTA, GA -- May 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced network printing software to enable Microsoft 
Windows NT system users to print directly to any of Digital's 
TCP/IP or DECnet network-connected printers (PrintServer 17/600, 
32, turboPrintServer 20, or DEClaser 5100 with optional network 
interface card).

      Digital's new Network Printing Software for Windows NT V5.0 
provides access to all of Digital's network printing features for 
desktop users in Windows NT operating environments. These 
features include bi-directional communication of printer and 
print job status in real-time, user selection of input and output 
tray, duplex (double-sided printing), simplex (single-sided 
printing), and automatic jam recovery -- all from remote 
locations.

     "The extension of Digital's network printing leadership to 
Windows NT environments demonstrates our commitment to open 
systems," said Larry Cabrinety, vice president of Digital's 
Components and Peripherals Business Unit.  "Desktop Microsoft 
Windows NT users will now be able to access the level of network 
printing that only Digital provides."

     Digital's Network Printing Software for Windows NT systems 
supports Digital's full line of PrintServer network printers 
which range in speed from 17 to 32 pages per minute, and the 8 
page-per-minute DEClaser 5100 with optional network card), and 
include 600 X 600 dpi and large format models.  The software is 
licensed from Digital at $98.  Shipments begin with the next 
release of Windows NT.

