                DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION OPENS
            DISK MANUFACTURING PLANT IN PENANG, MALAYSIA


     106,000 Square Foot Facility Will Help Meet Strong Demand
                     For Digital's Disk Drives


PENANG, Malaysia -- June 8, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the opening of its new disk drive manufacturing 
plant in Penang, Malaysia.  The 106,000 square foot facility, 
located on 9.7 acres in the Bayon Lepas Industrial Park, contains 
the latest in manufacturing environments, including a Class 100 
clean room.  The plant is designed for future expansion to 376,000 
square feet.  Manufacturing activities at the Penang facility begin
this week.

     "Digital has made a significant investment in dollars and in 
personnel to establish a world-class disk drive manufacturing 
facility in Penang," said Charles F. Christ, vice president of 
Digital's Storage Business Unit.  "Today's opening marks a new 
phase in our intention to continue the successful growth of the OEM 
storage business."

     He added that because of its highly skilled labor force, 
Penang is an ideal location for manufacturing high-quality disk 
drive products.  "We'll have the immediate ability to produce disk 
drives meeting Digital's high-quality standards, with room for 
increased capacity as worldwide demand for our products continues 
to grow rapidly."

     Bill Lowe, vice president of manufacturing for Digital's 
Storage Business Unit, added, "As a leading supplier of high-
capacity, high-performance disk drives to the OEM market, we are 
committed to meeting the high-volume requirements of our customers 
with competitive products from the Penang plant."

