            DIGITAL NAMES ROBERT RENNICK VICE PRESIDENT
                  OF STORAGE SUBSYSTEMS BUSINESS

        
MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 9, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it has appointed Robert Rennick to the 
position of vice president and general manager of the Storage 
Subsystems Business.  Rennick, who reports to Charles F. Christ, 
vice president of the Storage Business Unit, will continue to be 
responsible for all aspects of Digital's Subsystems Business, 
which includes not only the highly successful StorageWorks product 
family, but a growing OEM and multiplatform storage solutions 
business as well. As general manager of Digital's Subsystems 
Business, Rennick has directed the design, acquisition, marketing, 
manufacture, sale and support of a broad range of hardware and 
software solutions for the storage and management of information, 
from desktop to datacenter. 

     "Bob Rennick has played a key role in the phenomenal growth 
and success of the Storage Business Unit over the past three 
years," said Christ. "Under his management, the StorageWorks 
product line has become the standard against which other storage 
subsystems are measured."

     "I'm excited about leading the innovative team that worked 
with our customers to create the StorageWorks family," said 
Rennick. "The industry has a tremendous appetite for high-quality 
modular storage arrays built on standards and, as a result, the 
Subsystems Business is one of the fastest-growing organizations 
within Digital. I look forward to the opportunity for even greater 
success for the StorageWorks product line, and for our 
multiplatform and OEM activities." 

     Rennick has 25 years of management experience in the computer 
and aerospace industries, the last 12 with Digital. He joined the 
Storage organization in 1984. He holds BA, BSEE, and MSEE degrees 
from Columbia University. 

