             DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW PERFORMANCE-ENHANCED
                         InfoServer PACKAGES


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 16, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it has enhanced its InfoServer product line, 
providing higher performance CD-ROM drives with its CD-ROM server 
packages, and offering a new packaged system aimed at publishing 
CD-ROMs. The InfoServer 1000 product family provides the 
easiest-to-use, most flexible solution in the industry for CD-ROM 
serving. The RRD43 double speed CD-ROM drive is a low-cost, 
innovative caddy-less system for CD mounting. The InfoServer 
Publisher solution is a low-cost, entry point, plug-and-play system 
with all the hardware and software necessary for customers to 
install and begin recording their own CDs in native file formats. 

InfoServer 1000 CD-ROM Servers

     Designed for CD-ROM serving, the InfoServer Librarian and 
InfoServer Local Area CD (LA CD) packages now incorporate Digital's 
new RRD43 2X CD-ROM drives.  The InfoServer VXT X-Window terminal 
server, when bundled with a CD drive, also will include this new 
device. These higher performing devices move Digital further into 
the competitive CD-ROM drive market by providing high quality, 
double-speed drives for all of Digital's CD-ROM solutions, including 
the InfoServer family of products.  Digital's InfoTower expansion 
cabinet also will incorporate the new RRD43 drives.  

InfoServer Publisher Package for Network Mastering CD-ROMs

     The InfoServer Publisher integrates the InfoServer 1000 with a 
CD-ROM drive, a hard disk and a CD reader. These components are 
housed in the InfoTower enclosure. The package includes the 
hardware, the InfoServer Server License, the InfoServer CD/R 
Function Access License and software, and the Infoserver Disk 
Function Access License and software. 

     According to InfoServer marketing manager Dale Rensing, 
"Customers can use the InfoServer Publisher for all their low-volume 
CD publishing needs. These may include software distribution to 
local or remote sites, replacing old microfiche solutions with CD 
solutions, distributing sales and marketing data and programs to 
remote sites offices, publishing regular updates to long internal 
documents, and for near-line storage of key data. The flexibility of 
the InfoServer 1000 makes it the most powerful server in the CD 
industry today." 

     The InfoServer Publisher is the lowest-cost integrated package 
available for low-volume CD publishing, utilizing the 5.25 inch JVC 
CD/R drive. It allows customers to master CDs for archiving, or for 
software and data distribution. It can be used with most major 
mastering (or formatting) software; it has been tested successfully 
with Young Mind's MakeDisk and Electroson GEAR. In addition, 
Electroson GEAR recently has created software to work specifically 
with InfoServer.

     InfoServer solutions can be integrated completely with 
StorageWorks subsystems. The popular family of StorageWorks products 
provides complete, cost-effective storage subsystems for multivendor 
environments. 

Pricing and Availability

All products are available now.

