          DIGITAL'S AVASTOR BUSINESS ANNOUNCES BREAKTHROUGH
            DISK DRIVE PERFORMANCE FOR DESKTOP COMPUTING


      New Capella Series Includes First Magneto-resistive Drive


SHREWSBURY, MA -- June 21, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation's 
newly named AVASTORt business today set new standards in desktop 
computing performance with the announcement of three disk drives in 
its new Capella Series of 3.5-inch, one-inch high, 5400 rpm 
products.  Designed for high-performance desktop computing 
applications, AVASTOR's Capella 3221 2.2 GB magneto-resistive (MR)
drive incorporates its advanced ASABETt silicon chip technology and 
provides the desktop industry's fastest net host user data transfer 
rate, of 7.5 MB per second, and seek time of 8 milliseconds (ms).  
In addition the drive provides one of the highest MTBF ratings of 
800,000 continuous operation hours.  The new Capella Series 3110 
(1.1 GB) and 3055 (550 MB) drives utilize inductive heads and 
incorporate patented ASABET technology to deliver leading MTBF 
ratings of 700,000 continuous operation hours, seek times of 8.5 ms 
and data transfer rates of 5.2 MB, at value prices.

     In a separate release today, Digital also announced that to 
further distinguish its leadership in the storage components 
industry, it renamed its OEM Storage Business AVASTOR and 
established a new Customer Resource Center hotline and bulletin 
board service to provide product support and information for its 
customers.  AVASTOR, which manufactures magnetic disks, DLT tape 
drives and solid state disk products, is an integral part of 
Digital's Storage Business Unit.  The Storage Business Unit, led 
by Charles Christ, also includes Digital's Heads, StorageWorks 
Solutions, and Video Interactive and Information Services businesses.

     "With the explosion of multimedia, video and networking 
applications, higher performance on the desktop is increasingly 
critical.  Our breakthrough MR disk drive is further evidence of our 
strategy to bring advanced storage technologies to desktop computing 
customers," said Jack Sharp, vice president of sales and marketing 
for Digital's AVASTOR business.  "These new products, combined with 
the AVASTOR identity, strengthen our commitment to leadership in
the market for high-performance, cost-effective storage components."

     All of AVASTOR's new drives are designed to meet the needs of 
high-performance desktop systems such as engineering workstations, 
desktop publishing, multimedia and networked file servers.  
According to International Data Corporation, the demand for 
high-performance 1 GB+ 3.5-inch disk drives more than tripled 
between 1992 and 1993.  As this strong growth continues, AVASTOR's 
traditional strengths in delivering high-performance storage 
components will enable it to provide products that lead the desktop 
industry in capacity, reliability and speed.

Setting New Performance Standards for the Desktop

     To enhance system performance, AVASTOR tailored its new ASABET 
technology for the desktop disk drive market.  The ASABET chip set, 
announced in November 1993, comprises industry-leading silicon that 
increases drive performance by providing very low SCSI command 
overhead and reduced bus execution times.

     "High-quality silicon and head technologies are the gating 
factors for disk drive success," said Peter Franklin, director of 
marketing for Digital's AVASTOR business.  "The ASABET silicon chip 
set, combined with advanced head technologies, have enabled us to 
answer desktop user demands for increased drive performance and 
durability at low component costs."

     In addition to ASABET, the following leading-edge technologies 
are incorporated into AVASTOR's new low-profile, Fast SCSI-2 Capella 
Series:

     o 	3D ROSE t(3-Dimensional Rotationally Optimized Seek 
        Execution), which reorders commands to minimize seek and 
        rotational delay, optimizing disk drive performance.

     o 	The largest cache (1.024 KB) available on the desktop 
        provides faster data access.

     o 	An optional Write Back Cache feature also results in faster 
        data access, as well as higher system throughput by 
        appending multiple consecutive write commands into a single 
        revolution write operation.

     o 	Embedded servo continuously compensates for temperature 
        changes and enhances desktop video applications such as 
        frame editing, by preventing disruptive calibrations during 
        data transfer.  Digital Equipment's 16 years of expertise 
        with this technology makes this the industry's most advanced 
        embedded servo.

     AVASTOR also optimized the design of its disk drive actuator 
mechanism, LSI circuits and processors for the desktop environment, 
to offer its new drives at value prices.

Raising the Reliability Bar

     The new AVASTOR drives also raise the standard for desktop 
storage reliability and lower the cost of ownership.  The MR and 
inductive head products' respective 800,000 and 700,000 continuous 
operation MTBF ratings outperform all desktop drives on the market 
when tested under the toughest conditions. The rates are based on 
24-hour-per-day, seven-day-per-week, continuous operation at 30x C.  
And, AVASTOR drives offer a 5-year warranty, compared to competitive 
desktop class drives of three years.

Pricing/Availability

     The Capella Series 3221 drives will be available in the fourth 
quarter of 1994.  The suggested evaluation unit price is $1,720.  
The Capella Series 3110 and 3055 drives will be available in the 
third quarter of 1994.  The suggested evaluation unit list prices 
are $1,125 and $765, respectively.

     A pilot line of the drives is currently underway in Digital 
Equipment's Shrewsbury, Massachusetts facility.  Initial production 
of evaluation units will commence in the company's Colorado Springs, 
Colorado facility and transition to the new Penang, Malaysia plant 
shortly thereafter.

     AVASTOR, a business of Digital Equipment Corporation, provides 
leading storage components for computer and subsystem vendors, 
resellers and distributor markets worldwide.  Headquartered in 
Shrewsbury, Massachusetts, AVASTOR develops and sells high-
performance magnetic disk drives, solid state disks, and DLT tape 
drives.  The industry's fastest growing disk manufacturer, AVASTOR 
leverages technologies, such as its performance-enhancing ASABET
silicon chip set, to provide storage components that set new 
standards in reliability, capacity and speed.
