          DIGITAL AND OPT PARTNER TO DELIVER AN INTEGRATED
           SOLUTION TO MINI-MILLS AND SPECIALTY PRODUCERS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 22, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Order Processing Technologies (OPT) today announced a 
partnership to market and implement RollCIM(R), an integrated, 
strategic information system that manages the full range of 
ordering and manufacturing information critical for producing and 
delivering low-cost, high-quality steel.  Running on the 
full range of Digital's OpenVMS VAX and Alpha AXP platforms, 
RollCIM helps companies boost their efficiency and productivity, 
and eliminates the time-consuming and costly procedure of 
customizing standard manufacturing software to fit the unique 
demands of steel mini-mills and specialty producers.

     "Metals producers sell and manufacture in unique ways," said 
Mike Lowery, President of OPT, "and their customers demand timely, 
quality information as well as quality products.  RollCIM addresses 
their specialized requirements for traceability, certification, 
costing, scrap, diversion and labeling."

     RollCIM consists of 16 software modules that automatically 
integrate and exchange data across company functions. It is designed 
to enhance control over metal product manufacturing processes, 
reduces data maintenance, shortens the product definition cycle, 
enhancing customer service, and improving administrative controls.  
RollCIM delivers leadership functionality in the areas of capacity 
planning, order management, packing and shipping, inventory and 
accounts receivable, quality and certification supporting ISO 9000, 
data collection, inventory and tracking, costing, specifications and 
routings, scheduling, material planning, plant maintenance, purchasing, 
stores inventory, payables, and general ledger.

     "Digital is pleased and proud to partner with OPT on this 
endeavor," stated Chuck Eichenlaub, Digital's Worldwide Industry 
Director for Metals and Glass.  "RollCIM is demonstrably the best 
software available for mini-mills and specialty producers. Building 
on Digital's worldwide networking, open client/server solutions, 
and systems integration, Digital and OPT offer users a unique, 
flexible solution that will ensure their competitive advantage well 
into the next century."

     RollCIM optimizes information flow and information access from 
start to finish.  When a customer places an order, RollCIM informs 
the order-taker when and where the order can be filled, thus 
reducing order-taking time from hours or days to minutes.  RollCIM 
then tracks every piece of information about the order as it moves 
through the plant --- from scrap sources and quality levels to 
location on the plant floor to delivery date.  It enables 
mini-mills and specialty producers to respond quickly to customer 
queries about manufacturing, quality, and shipping.

     RollCIM supports multi-site, multi-division, multi-legal 
entity, and multi-currency operations, and exporting.

     Digital is an authorized reseller of the RollCIM product 
family, and showcases RollCIM at its Metals and Glass Solution 
Center in Pittsburgh, PA.

     Order Processing Technologies was founded in 1982.  Its sole 
business is to develop and support RollCIM.  OPT is committed to 
making RollCIM the finest integrated manufacturing system for roll 
manufacturing, which includes the metal, glass, film, and paper 
industries.  OPT is located in Framingham, Massachusetts, at 
(508) 370-4500.  Its Internet address is INFO@ROLLCIM.COM.  OPT 
Europe is headquartered in Bristol, U.K., at (44) 0272 256286.  
The Internet address is INFO@LANCE.ROLLCIM.CO.UK.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
