                      67 Alpha AXP Systems ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 22, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation has 
been awarded a complex 8.1 million dollar systems integration 
project with NEC Corporation to build a sophisticated weather 
forecasting and climatic data processing center for the National 
Space Research Institute (INPE) in Brazil.  Digital will serve as a 
subcontractor to NEC; NEC will provide a SX3-Model 12R 
supercomputer.  

     In addition to systems integration services, Digital will 
provide through its Brazil operation several hardware and software 
products, including 67 systems based on the world's fastest 64-bit 
microprocessor -- Alpha AXP. The Alpha AXP systems will serve as the 
scientific subsystem for the NEC supercomputer and for the 
telecommunications, archive and network systems.

     The partnership with NEC reflects Digital's expertise in 
integrating highly complex systems in association with other major 
international vendors. As the systems integrator, Digital will 
manage the integration of products and services from 23 
international vendors.

     The project will result in a complete information system for 
the Weather Forecasting and Climatic Studies Center (CPTEC).

