      DIGITAL ANNOUNCES SUPPORT FOR ORACLE PARALLEL PROCESSING


      ... Oracle7 Release 7.1 Now Available on Digital Systems
 

MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 22, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced early availability of Oracle7 release 7.1 on 
Digital's VAX systems with production availability on both Alpha 
AXP and VAX systems in July. 

     Oracle7 release 7.1 offers a wide range of parallel processing 
capabilities including key features such as Parallel Query, and 
Parallel Recovery in addition to dynamic load balancing for 
efficient scaling.  The Parallel Query feature automatically 
decomposes SQL queries into tasks that are executed in multiple
processes across parallel processors.  Parallel Recovery 
transparently exploits parallel processors to recover failed 
database quickly. 

     "Early customer sites have found that the new functionality of 
release 7.1 complements Oracle's traditional SMP scaling on Digital 
systems.  Our customers will also experience exceptional 
opportunities for expansion and availability with both Digital's 
UNIX and OpenVMS clusters," said Max Mayer, Digital's vice
president for software alliances. 

     "Oracle and Digital have been working together closely on 
Oracle7 release 7.1," said Beatriz Infante, vice president Digital 
Products Division, Oracle Corporation.  "Much of the base 
development for 7.1 and key beta sites were on Digital platforms.  
The combination of 7.1 and Alpha AXP systems will set a new 
standard in open, parallel and scalable computing, which customers 
are demanding.  Customers seeking open, relational information 
systems alternatives will find the Oracle/Digital solution is 
superb," said Infante. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
