           DIGITAL NAMES E.C. PROKOPIS AS VICE PRESIDENT
                      AND CORPORATE CONTROLLER


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 23, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the election of E.C. "Mick" Prokopis as vice 
president and corporate controller, effective immediately.

     Before becoming Digital's corporate controller, Prokopis, 51, 
was executive vice president of the Ziff Corporation. Previously, 
he was vice president of Budgeting at Digital, chief financial 
officer at Lotus Development Corporation, and vice president and 
chief financial officer at United Technologies Corporation's Mostek 
Corporation. He also held major financial roles at The Mitre 
Corporation's Washington Operations.

     "Mick brings to Digital more than 25 years of proven business 
and financial leadership experience from both inside and outside 
the computer industry," said Vincent J. Mullarkey, Digital's vice 
president and chief financial officer. "His strengths in business 
planning, budgeting, controls and operations are critical to our 
determination to accelerate the company's progress toward sustained 
profitability." 

     A Vietnam veteran, Prokopis holds a bachelor's degree in 
Business Administration from the University of Massachusetts in 
Amherst.

