              DIGITAL SIMPLIFIES DECHUB 90 MANAGEMENT


         ...popular network hub product easily upgraded...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 27, 1994 -- In keeping with its strategy to 
make network management easier, less expensive and more flexible 
without sacrificing functionality, Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that customers can perform SNMP management with or 
without a DECbridge 90 in the DEChub 90 line of networking 
products. This means that the cost of managing a DEChub 90 with 
repeaters can be reduced by 50%. 

     Bill Seaver, Network Management marketing manager, notes, "It 
became clear that not all users needed to segment their network 
with bridges. Thus, we modified the firmware in the DECagent 90 so 
the bridge was no longer required.  This is another example of how 
Digital's DEChub products provide flexibility without sacrificing 
functionality." 

     The upgrade kit is shipping now in all DECagent 90s.  Existing 
DECagent 90 users can upgrade, at no charge, by copying the upgrade 
kit from the Internet via anonymous ftp at ftp.digital.com under/
pub/DEC/hub900.

Pricing and ordering information 

Upgrade kits from DECagent V1.0 or from V1.1:


     Model No. 	      Description		       Price 

     QB-MQEAA-SA      Agent/Brg 90V/V SRL TK50 PKG     $200.00       
     QB-MQEAB-SA      Agent/Brg 90U/R SRL TK50 PKG     $200.00       


NOTE:  These part numbers also include an upgrade for the DECbridge 
90 to version 3.1  (the version compatible with DECagent 90 V2.0) 
and DECndu Plus Load Utility.  

