             DIGITAL TAKES NEW TACK BY APPOINTING ANIXTER
                      AS ITS NETWORK DISTRIBUTOR
     

Hong Kong, China -- June 24, 1994 -- In a breakaway move aimed at
reinforcing its position as a leader in networking technologies and
products, Digital Asia has signed a strategic deal with Anixter Inc to
distribute its networking products throughout the Asia Pacific region
at significantly lower prices.
  
     "Signing a regional distributorship deal is in line with Digital's 
corporate strategy of embracing channel partners in Asia," said John 
Winchester, Asia Region Director of Network Products for Digital. 
"Although we've been strong within our existing customer base and are 
among the top three networking vendors in the region, we realise the 
urgency of working with channel partners to increase our market share."
  
     Anixter, a company that focusses specifically on reselling
networking products, recently opened a state-of-the-art distribution
hub in Hong Kong that is permanently on line to its 150 offices
throughout the United States, Europe and the Pacific Rim headquarters
in Singapore. The warehouse provides accurate inventory information
and efficient sales and support systems, achieving a level of
logistical support seldom found in the region.
  
     "Our worldwide distribution network handles more than one million 
transactions a day," said Steve Kung, Anixter's Managing Director for 
North Asia. "Our computer system in Quarry Bay enables our sales staff 
to locate the desired products immediately so they can be shipped in 
the shortest possible time. We welcome this expansion into Asia of our
partnership with Digital, whose networking products are 
top-of-the-line."
  
     Added Winchester; "The Asia Pacific region represents about 15 per 
cent of Digital's worldwide revenue. Our networking products' revenue 
will contribute approximately US$600 million in sales throughout the 
world. While Asia represents a lot of opportunities, it also represents
a vast and diverse territory to cover effectively.
  
     "Anixter is one of the biggest distributors of networking products
in the world. The size of the market, not to mention the fact that it's 
booming, means we must rely on channel sales and Anixter is our 
preferred partner."
  
     Kung said Anixter and Digital will build on a relationship which
has already proved successful in the United States, where the two 
companies have combined to sell Digital's networking products for over 
eight years, and in Europe for the past six years.

     "We're going to work together to recruit dealers in a new twist,
what we call a double relationship," said Kung. "We'll send out people
from both companies to make sales calls and to educate dealers. To
help these dealers differentiate themselves in the marketplace, we're
going to offer them a chance to participate in the Digital's networking 
product certification programme, which ranges from basic networking all
the way up to planning a network from scratch".
  
     Anixter specialises in the distribution of products for the 
transmission of data, voice and multimedia applications, as well as 
electrical and electronic wire and cable. Anixter serves its customers 
by providing technical assistance and solutions using a variety of 
products from the world's leading manufacturers. Regionally, Anixter 
has offices in Hong Kong, Singapore, Malaysia and China with plans to 
open others soon in Indonesia and Thailand. Anixter, a wholly owned 
subsidiary of Itel Corporation, had 1993 revenues of US1.3 billion.
  
     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide
information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP platforms, storage,
networking, software and services, together with industry-focused
solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
today's global marketplace. A US$14 billion company, Digital employs
more than 80,000 people in 100 countries. In Asia, it operates in 14
countries in addition to Japan and has manufacturing plants in India,
Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore and Taiwan.
