                  DIGITAL ANNOUNCES WIDE CARRIAGE
                  PC PRINTER WITH COLOR CAPABILITY


NEW YORK, NY -- June 28, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a low-priced, wide-carriage dot matrix forms 
printer with color capability, priced at $479.  The new DECwriter 
195 24-wire wide-carriage PC printer includes a Windows 3.1 printer 
driver, full documentation and a two-year warranty.  This PC 
printer autosenses between its resident Epson LQ-1170 and IBM 
Proprinter XL24e emulations, prints 360 X 360 dpi resolution at up 
to 300 cps, includes two resident scalable and eight additional 
fonts, and at 49.5 dBA has a noise level as quiet as a laser or 
inkjet printer to facilitate use in department, small business and 
home office environments.  The announcement was made at the PC EXPO 
Conference, which opened here today at the Jacob Javits Convention 
Center.

     The DECwriter 195 PC printer handles either fanfold or 
cutsheet paper, labels, envelopes, and up to 4-part carbonless 
forms.  Its user-installable $79 optional color kit enables it to 
print in seven colors on all of these media.

     "Digital's DECwriter 195 printer directly connects to PC 
systems and supports printing from windows-based applications that 
contain graphics, color and scalable fonts," said Larry Cabrinety, 
Vice President of Digital's Components and Peripherals Business 
Unit.

     With its simple-to-use LCD control panel with color display 
keyed to color-coded documentation, the DECwriter 195 PC printer 
enables the user to easily configure, store and recall the most 
commonly-needed user setups.

     The DECwriter 195 PC printer is priced in single quantities at 
$479; there is a 5% discount on pallet shipments of 12 units, 
resulting in a $445.50 price per printer.  Deliveries begin in 
July.  Options include a color kit for 7-color printing, $79, 128 
Kbyte expansion RAM memory, $80, automatic sheet feeder, $249.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
