            DIGITAL NAMES JOE CANNIZZARO VICE PRESIDENT,
                         WORLDWIDE MARKETING,
              COMPONENTS AND PERIPHERALS BUSINESS UNIT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 28, 1994 -- Digital Equipment today announced 
that it has named Joe Cannizzaro Vice President of worldwide 
marketing of the company's Components and Peripherals Business Unit.  
The Components and Peripherals business includes the design, 
manufacture and marketing of all of Digital's video text and X 
window terminals, desktop and network printers, Technical and 
Component OEM organizations, Corporate Licensing, Private Label and 
retail sales activities, along with related accessories, supplies 
and software products.  A 19-year veteran of Digital's engineering 
and manufacturing organizations, Cannizzaro reports to Larry 
Cabrinety, Vice President of Digital's Components and Peripherals 
Business Unit.

      In this position, Cannizzaro will provide the focal point for 
all marketing activities worldwide for the Components and 
Peripherals Business unit.  His role will continue to expand as the 
business unit articulates its business and marketing strategies and 
implementation plans.  Cannizzaro's role encompasses the strategy 
and operational direction of the business unit's marketing 
organization and programs in the U.S., Europe and Asia/Pacific 
including advertising, direct marketing, trade shows, external 
events, public relations, analyst relations, customer relations, 
sales tools, product literature and training.  Cannizzaro will serve 
as the senior marketing liaison to marketing functions internal and 
external to Digital and work collaboratively with the business 
segments in the Components and Peripherals business unit to achieve 
established business goals.

      Cannizzaro's previous positions at Digital include Group 
Engineering Manager in the LES Engineering Process and Technology 
Organization, Project and Manufacturing Manager for the Greenville, 
South Carolina PWB Manufacturing facility, Group Engineering Manager 
for PWB Operations, and Group Manager, Marketing Operations/New 
Ventures Group in the Video, Image and Print Systems (VIPS) group 
prior to its formation as the Components and Peripherals Business 
Unit.								    

      Prior to joining Digital, Cannizzaro held engineering 
positions with IBM.  He is a graduate of Long Island University, 
Lesley College and the INSEAD International Executive Program in 
Fontainbleau, France.  He is a long-time resident of Harvard, 
Massachusetts, with his wife Dolores and two sons, Joseph and 
Christopher.                                                        

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
