                  DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION

                           FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:  PrintServer 17/600 Network Printer for NetWare
               Environments


OVERVIEW:

Digital's PrintServer 17/600 Network Printer for NetWare 
Environments is a Novell Tested and Approved printer which 
handles complex documents containing images and multi-font text 
at 17 pages per minute and 600 X 600 dpi resolution in print 
volumes up to 70,000 impressions per month.  It is a departmental 
printer with all of the networking capabilities, real-time 
two-way communications and the paper handling flexibility of 
Digital's PrintServer products, but with the size, footprint and 
price associated with desktop laser printers.
          
The PrintServer 17/600 Network Printer for NetWare Environments 
supports NetWare V3.11, V3.12 and V4.0X environments.  In 
addition, the printer supports a wide range of operating 
environments, accepting print jobs from any desktop device in an 
Ethernet environment, whether local or remote, running  Novell 
NetWare, Windows NT, AT&T Unison, HP-UX, IBM AIX, Pyramid OSx, 
SCO UNIX, Sequent Dynix, Silicon Graphics IRIS, Solaris, SunOS, 
UNISYS System V, DEC OSF/1 AXP, ULTRIX, OpenVMS (VAX and Alpha) 
or (via PATHWORKS, NetWare or third party products), DOS, OS/2 or 
Macintosh systems -- all simultaneously.


KEY FEATURES AND BENEFITS:
          
o NetWare tested and approved.

o Direct Ethernet attachment with ThinWire or Twisted-Pair 
  interface.
          
o Two-way real-time communication of print job status alerts 
  users of start of print job, successful completion of print 
  job, out of paper, and more, even from remote geographies.  It 
  provides printer status messages to users or system managers,
  communicating job status messages (print job complete) to
  users and printer status (paper and toner outages, jams) to
  system managers.
          
o Central system management provides system administrators with
  a full range of accounting information, enabling them to
  monitor printer usage, learn of printer conditions such as out
  of paper or toner, control printing privileges, download
  forms, fonts, logos, software and printer enhancements, and
  meet the changing demands, whether local or remote, from a 
  central location.

o Simplex (single-sided) or duplex (double-sided, optional $635)
  printing capability, user selectable.
          
o Resident Adobe PostScript Level 2 and HP PCL-5 Page Description 
  Languages (PDLs).  Translator on UNIX systems for ASCII.  
  Translators on ULTRIX systems for DEC ANSI/SIXEL, HP PCL-4, 
  TEKTRONIX 4010/4014, and ReGIS.  Translators on OpenVMS systems 
  for DEC ANSI/SIXEL, HP PCL-4, ASCII, TEKTRONIX 4010/4014, IBM 
  Proprinter and ReGIS.
          
o 43 Resident Adobe fonts, ensuring full Apple LaserWriter font
  capability.  16 PCL fonts are also resident.  Optional fonts, 
  which may be downloaded from a central site, are available.

o Handles specified labels, envelopes, transparencies, letterhead 
  and cutsheet paper in weights up to 24 lbs (90 g/m2) in sizes:  
  letter, legal, executive, A, A4 and B5.

o Automatically converts non-PostScript to PostScript format.
          
o Supports multiple network protocols:  DECnet and TCP/IP 
  protocols simultaneously.

o Two standard input trays with 500 sheet capacity each, one
  output tray with 500 sheet (face-down; 50 sheet total face-up)
  capacity.  Optional 1500-sheet input feeder ($585), 3000-sheet
  output stacker/stand ($1,195).  Optional envelope feeder (100
  envelopes, $445)
          
o Enables banner pages to separate print jobs that can be
  customized to include information such as  corporate logos.

o Resident 16 MByte memory expandable to 32 MBytes.
          
o Prints bar codes, forms, logos and signatures.
          
o Includes number-up (up to 100) capability for printing
  multiple images per side of a sheet of paper enabling paper
  cost savings and facilitating document review.
          
o Footprint:  19.0 inches H X 17.9 inches W X 22.4 inches D (483 
  mm X 454 mm X 570 mm).  Weight:  98 lbs (44.5 kg)
          

PRICING AND AVAILABILITY:
          
The PrintServer 17/600 NetWare network printer is priced at 
$4,695 in single quantities and is available in August, 1994.

Option Pricing:   
          Input sheet feeder (1500 sheets)   $585
          Envelope feeder (100 envelopes)    $445
          Duplex Upgrade Kit                 $635
          Memory (4 MBytes)                  $395
