                   DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
              NAMES WILLIAM F. ARMITAGE VICE PRESIDENT
             OF EMBEDDED AND REALTIME PRODUCTS BUSINESS
 

MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 29, 1994 -- DIGITAL EQUIPMENT Corporation 
today announced the appointment of WILLIAM F. Armitage to vice 
president of the Embedded and Realtime Products Business.  Armitage 
will manage overall worldwide operations, including engineering, 
sales, marketing and business development.  The Embedded and 
Realtime Products Business is a segment of the Components and 
Peripherals Business Unit within Digital Equipment Corporation.

     "With more than twenty years of high technology business 
development and management experience, Bill provides the strategic 
and operation leadership skills necessary to build and maintain a 
high-growth operation," said Larry Cabrinety, vice president of the 
Components and Peripherals Business Unit, Digital Equipment 
Corporation.

     Armitage joined Digital in 1981.  He has held various senior 
management positions at Digital, including his most recent role as 
director of the Embedded and Realtime Products Business.  Prior to 
joining Digital, Armitage held management positions at General 
Electric Company.

     Armitage holds a Master of Science degree in management from 
the Massachusetts Institute of Technology Sloan School of 
Management.  He received a Master of Science and Bachelor of 
Science degree, both in electrical engineering, from Brown 
University.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
